# comp[AI]on — Alembic migrations

Schema migrations for the SQLite database. Managed by Alembic; applied
automatically on app startup via `backend/db.py`'s `init_db()`.

## Layout
- `alembic.ini` ............ lives at repo root (uses `%(here)s/backend/migrations`)
- `env.py` ................. wired to `backend.db.engine` + `SQLModel.metadata`
- `versions/` .............. revision scripts (named `NNNN_slug.py`)
- `script.py.mako` ......... revision template

## Common commands
Run from repo root with `PYTHONPATH` set (env.py imports `backend.*`):

```powershell
set PYTHONPATH=C:\Users\danyo\Desktop\Uni\comp[AI]on

# Create a new migration from model changes
backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"

# Apply pending migrations
backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head

# Roll back one revision
backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic downgrade -1

# Show current revision
backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic current

# Show migration history
backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic history --verbose
```

## Notes
- `render_as_batch=True` is enabled in `env.py` for SQLite batch ALTER support.
- Always review autogenerated migrations — SQLite cannot do some ALTERs
  in-place and autogenerate may miss or misrender certain diffs.
- `init_db()` auto-adopts pre-Alembic databases by stamping the baseline
  revision then upgrading, so existing user data is preserved.
